      "conf": "VERIFIED · VENDOR DATA",
      "dek": "Overnight the market pulled two ways and it has now settled upward. Japan closed 1.30% higher at 66,364.20, led by the firms that build chip-making machines rather than the chipmakers themselves: Tokyo Electron finished up 4.82%. Hong Kong cut its loss from 1.58% to 1.19%, Europe opened higher, and US S&P 500 futures turned from slightly down to 0.14% up. For someone holding for years this is a tone, not an event: no company release or official figure this morning explains the machine makers' jump, and Germany's better business survey landed yesterday, not today. The real test is the US factory orders report at 13:30 UK.",
