      "conf": "VERIFIED · VENDOR DATA",
      "dek": "The VIX, the market's fear gauge, is 15.60, down 0.07 from Thursday's close of 15.67. It has traded in a range of just 15.60 to 15.61 so far, which says the options market has no strong view this morning rather than that it is calm by conviction. On the BuyTrigger ladder that is the normal band, 15 to 20: it sits 0.60 above the calm line and 14.40 below the 30 mark where the system reads a buy window as open. Nothing on that ladder changes today. Watch whether the US factory orders figure at 13:30 UK moves it.",
