      "conf": "VENDOR DATA · EARNINGS DATE SINGLE SOURCE",
      "dek": "Micron traded at $1,089.54 in the overnight session, up 0.83%, which is $8.50 above the highest price it reached during Thursday's regular session. That is the third edition in a row in which the stock has set a new mark while New York slept, and it is the same memory-chip chain that carried Tokyo's machine makers higher. For a long-term holder the question is whether the price is running ahead of the earnings: Micron's fiscal fourth-quarter results are expected on 30 September, though I cannot confirm that date at a company source. The run does not hold the trigger levels, so the element is words only.",
