      "conf": "VERIFIED · REGULATOR RECORD",
      "dek": "On Thursday Oracle fell 3.47% and Blue Owl, a large private-credit lender to data-centre projects, fell 3.65% on the same day. I checked Blue Owl's own SEC record for the first time this morning: its newest filing is dated 14 September, eleven days ago. Oracle's newest is 23 September, six documents accepted between 23:06 and 23:22 UTC, with nothing on 24 or 25 September. So two companies whose shares moved together have both said nothing. Both edged up overnight, Oracle to $140.27. Until one of them files, the fall has no document behind it, which is a reason to wait rather than to conclude.",
