      "conf": "VERIFIED · VENDOR DATA",
      "dek": "Oil fell to $92.39 overnight, below the $92.69 low I reported at 06:30, then took most of it back and now trades at $93.41, down 1.27% on the day against Thursday's $94.61 close. That is a round trip of about 1.1% off the bottom in a few hours. Cheaper oil is a small help to company profit margins and to inflation figures, which is part of why European shares opened firmer. But a barrel that swings a dollar either way before London is properly awake is telling you about thin trading, not about supply. Watch whether it holds above $93 into the US open.",
