      "conf": "VERIFIED · PRIMARY",
      "dek": "The US Treasury's official yield page still shows Thursday's figures: the 10-year government bond yields 5.18%, the 30-year 5.47% and the 2-year 4.87%. There is no row for today yet, which is normal before the US market opens, because the page updates after the close. Thursday was the third day running in which long-dated yields rose faster than short ones, and that makes borrowing more expensive for the companies funding data centres. For someone holding shares for years, that is slow pressure worth tracking rather than a day's news. Today's figures arrive this evening; the question is whether 5.18% holds.",
